"""Pinned convex height smoothing on the final direct-quad geometry.

Positive mean-value corner weights use actual planar angles and edge lengths.
Their normalized sum reproduces linear functions at interior vertices even on
irregular quads. No triangles, optimization library or Python update handler is
used. The finite iteration count is a heuristic, not a slope/C1 guarantee.
"""
from . import boundary_quad_bridge_nodes as bridge


